  "outcome": "completed",
  "summary": "Second-pass amendment of the conversion-boundary design. Streaming replaces syntax-only plain-ASCII reuse with converted-segment reuse at closed-container blank-line boundaries plus spliced publication by identity (3,730/3,730 prefix-equivalent previews; rich 50 KB parse 24.6 to 0.72 s and publish 88.3 to 22.2 s). Property loss warns and content loss rejects, keeping Markdown export and AI serialization working on aligned, styled or pasted documents; Link HTML import stops inventing target _blank. preserve() claims stay for custom encoders behind a round-trip conformance harness; list accounting is fixed. Migration neutralizes legacy unsafe values instead of rejecting documents; the navigation floor blocks script-capable schemes while allowedSchemes keeps widening. DOCX source eligibility and paste feedback delivery move to their own plans. Plite per-transaction publication cost is a new separate owner.",
  "proof": {
    "state": "partial",
    "evidence": [
      {
        "path": "docs/research/probes/2026-09-28-conversion-boundary/amendment/stream-correctness.json",
        "sha256": "246ffac546e6778ee7d93538367fe9c3b6109bcfcec59b8d9528175b8e827978",
        "claim": "3,730/3,730 incremental previews deep-equal a fresh partial parse across 26 fixtures x 26 chunkings, including lists, fences, math, tags, tables, CJK and definitions."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/research/probes/2026-09-28-conversion-boundary/amendment/stream-benchmark.json",
        "sha256": "b4079f3a433cb2129a4b2d5edb35874945ddcbb0cb09cbe9cceeeaae8fba89a5",
        "claim": "Rich and CJK 10 KB (three alternating pairs) and 50 KB (one pair): parse and publication reductions with identical previews and published values asserted."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/research/probes/2026-09-28-conversion-boundary/amendment/roundtrip-verify.json",
        "sha256": "1d86c87fb9fe1a557e7da3b5c46d7a43704a969f4049da38add9cfdbb52d5b91",
        "claim": "Round-trip accounting over 44 fixtures: six unreported list indent/listStart losses, zero false positives; text round trip costs 4.7x serialize."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/research/probes/2026-09-28-conversion-boundary/amendment/loss-severity.json",
        "sha256": "13d7a0d943391e74fbbd338de0c7d504fc811ce9593e36bd5954454bd9527900",
        "claim": "Aligned, line-height, text-indent and HTML-pasted link documents export today with warnings; the pasted link carries an invented target _blank."
      },
      {
        "path": "docs/research/probes/2026-09-28-conversion-boundary/amendment/REPORT.md",
        "sha256": "6c381a0d866bebb245782226ba4c866779899468eb3b3a29250108a3e3e6568d",
        "claim": "Commands, results, splice profile (48 ms tail splice at 1,179 top-level nodes in Plite change application) and limits."
      }
    ],
    "limits": "Design amendment only; no product code changed. Timings are headless on a shared host (load 4-13); 50 KB has one pair. The probe parser is disposable and lacks invalidation on mapping/plugin-state changes and aggregate limits, which S5 still owes. Browser and consumer matrices are not run. Plite per-transaction publication cost is identified, not fixed."
  },
